  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Osra (Family)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Egypt):  The Osra (&quot;Family&quot;) activity aims to improve family health outcomes for Egyptian families by increasing the use of quality voluntary family planning and reproductive health (FP/RH) services and empowering women. Osra will support and contribute to the Government of Egypt&apos;s (GOE) National Population Strategy 2015-2030 and the three-year National Project for Family Development (2021-2023). The Osra project will strengthen high-impact practices in family planning and incorporate innovative, promising approaches to improve family health outcomes. .The Mission will jointly work with the Ministry of Health and Population (MOHP), the National Population Council (NPC), and potentially other Ministries in a multi-sectoral endeavor to achieve National Population Strategy milestones. Quality of, access to, and demand for voluntary family planning and reproductive health services are central to Osra. The activity will strengthen health systems and address women&apos;s equal participation in decision-making to improve the quality of life of families..</narrative>
  </description>
